# ==============================================================================
# Nexus Environment Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local frontend development.
# Do NOT commit `.env` or `.env.local` with real values.
#
# SECURITY NOTES:
# 1. Public Frontend Variables (`VITE_*`):
#    Vite embeds every variable prefixed with `VITE_` directly into the client
#    JavaScript bundle. Only place public identifiers and publishable keys here.
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase project URL (public).
#    - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Supabase anonymous/publishable key protected by
#      Row Level Security (RLS) policies (public).
#    - VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: Google OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID (public).
#
# 2. Server-Only Secrets (NEVER add `VITE_` prefix or put in frontend env):
#    Configure these strictly as Supabase Edge Function secrets (`supabase secrets set`)
#    or backend/Vercel server-side environment variables:
#    - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (bypasses RLS)
#    - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#    - GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#    - GOOGLE_DRIVE_REDIRECT_URI (e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app/auth/google-drive/callback)
#    - DRIVE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY (base64-encoded 32-byte AES-256-GCM key)
# ==============================================================================

# --- Public Client Variables (Frontend) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# --- Server-Only Reference (Set via `supabase secrets set`, NEVER prefix with VITE_) ---
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_REDIRECT_URI=
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_REDIRECT_URI=
# DRIVE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
